speechtext:
I think not, because (b), as I read it, only makes reference to restraining or injuring the export business of a domestic competitor who is not party to a conspiracy. I am talking about people who are party to a conspiracy if an expansion and decline of business take place within the conspiracy. Subparagraph (b) reads:
-has restrained or injured or is likely to restrain or injure the export business of any domestic competitor who is not a party to the conspiracy, combination, agreement or arrangement;
So with regard to the case I dealt with which might arise, the minister says it could be dealt with under (a), or if not that it could be dealt with under (b). I submit that is not correct because (b) only deals with people outside the conspiracy.
